@@@ note
The marker check has to walk up to the paragraph's immediate parent, not just any
ancestor, so a nested blockquote's own alert is recognised independently of the quote
wrapping it.

@@@ input
> Outer commentary that sits above the nested callout.
>
> > [!TIP]
> > A nested alert still keeps its marker line, however deep the blockquote goes.

